WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:02.980
Okay, we're recording!

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.870
What should I talk about?

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.340
Maybe about why you were in prison?

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.420
Hmm.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:22.870
I was an athlete chosen 
as an Olympic candidate.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.760
Wow.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.610
It was for the pole vault 
in track-and-field.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.180
I was really on track to land it, too.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:38.700
But, one day, a slasher came out of nowhere 
and tried to murder my girlfriend.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.950
I tracked him down and beat him up for that.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.640
He just happened to die on me,

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.660
so I got arrested for it.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.500
My weapon?

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.460
I made my spear myself.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:01.330
I can use that spear to pole vault up 
and attack that way, too.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.300
Okay, next!

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.410
Fisherman!

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.730
I used to be a fisherman.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:14.360
I got in a fight with my fellow fishermen 
and accidentally killed one,

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.860
so I was thrown in the slammer.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.600
I can cast nets to capture Gibia,

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.720
or hook them with my fishing rod.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.230
I can use a sword, too.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:32.360
I-I'm a p-professional!
A professional with explosives!

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:38.160
I-I can cast bombs far away 
using this guy's fishing rod, too!

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.850
I-It's difficult to produce bombs on my own

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.300
now that there a-aren't 
a lot of materials left in the world.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.890
Wh-Why was I arrested?

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:57.360
I-I made a bomb to get back 
at our horrid government

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.500
a-and someone tipped them off!

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.890
Hmm...

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.480
<b>"New Allies"</b>

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.490
Whoa, what is this?

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:47.620
That's a huge castle.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.450
Is this our destination?

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:55.680
Yes.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.760
Once we turn here, 
the research center is just up ahead.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:16.850
That's...

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:25.360
Christ, there are Gibia everywhere!

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.380
We knew it would be this way.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:32.750
It'll only be harder to 
get inside once night falls.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:35.670
We have to go through.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.300
There are many of those that 
my sword won't work on, as well.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.720
Maybe we should pull back for now 
and come back later?

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.540
Let's not go in right now...

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.770
We'll have to go in there 
one way or another, though.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:59.820
Waiting around won't 
bring others to help us.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.480
Let's go.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:08.950
Even though we might get wiped out 
trying to fight that many Gibia.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.060
Sensui.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:25.860
Hmm?

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.290
The old man isn't with us anymore,

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.250
but I've got your back.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:41.990
We're both used to fights with
the odds stacked against us, right?

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.040
What?

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.910
You're right.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:55.950
I'll place my life in your hands.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.300
<i>I can't let anyone else die.</i>

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:05.210
<i>Even if it costs me my own life!</i>

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.830
Those guys again?

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:27.680
Your father never learns, does he?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.020
At a time like this?!

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:33.700
This time I'll be the one to get him!

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:41.550
No other choice.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.800
I'll deal with the Gibia.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.950
You two handle them.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:50.050
Get to it, you all!

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.280
<i>No way...</i>

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:04.870
<i>Why do people still have to 
attack each other after all this?!</i>

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.220
H-Here I go!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.370
What?!

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:44.360
What do they think they're doing?!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.640
We owe you all our lives.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.590
It would go against our code 
if we didn't repay that debt,

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.210
so we're here to help.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:24.640
Let's go!

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.010
Yeah!

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.090
Sensui!

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:28.980
Yeah!

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:08.200
Yes!

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:22.860
What?! Those guys aren't half bad!

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.210
Let's go, Kenroku!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:25.910
Yeah!

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.400
Doctor, are you okay?!

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:47.780
Yes.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:11.240
Guren!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.170
Come here!

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.680
I know, boss!

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.440
Eat this!

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.120
Is your injury okay?

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:17.170
Oh, it's still too early for me to be 
dragging the young ones down.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.060
It's just a scratch.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.210
I didn't get stung.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:28.160
Your help saved us.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.420
If you need people like us,

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:41.130
then we'll give you as much help as it takes.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:45.220
Wherever the boss goes, his men will follow.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:49.600
Hopefully we can all get along, Samurai-san.

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:52.310
Hmph.

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:59.240
I'm so glad!

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.960
This is great news!

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:03.670
Isn't it, Ayame?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:07.240
Looks like we'll have 
some good sake tonight!

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.920
<i>I finally made it this far.</i>

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:57.070
We call those creatures Gibia.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:58.950
They used to be human.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.010
Once you're infected by the Gibia's poison,

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:05.080
the cells in your body 
begin abnormal replication,

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:07.830
altering the human chromosomes

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:10.220
and causing metamorphosis 
into a monstrous form.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:14.090
That's why we're researching 
a cure right now,

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:17.730
a drug to turn Gibia back into humans.

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:27.920
Yeah, I'm going to complete the vaccine 
to restore Gibia into people!

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:36.680
I'm almost there...

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.690
Ah! That's...!

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.790
Katsu curry.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.780
Again?

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:47.970
Again.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.210
K-Katsu curry is really delicious!

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.570
Jeez.

00:13:56.900 --> 00:14:00.340
I wish the old man could 
have eaten some, too.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:01.730
Yeah.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.020
<i>Yukinojyo-san...</i>

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.660
Wait, this meat...

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:11.900
Yeah! It's good!

00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:14.410
What's wrong?

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:20.380
It might look a little bad, 
but it'll give you stamina.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:25.760
I-It's from the cafeteria here,
 so it's safe.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.010
It's not meat from them.

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.680
Of course it isn't.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:34.040
Yeah, this isn't bad.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:36.560
This is spicy.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.710
What kind of spice is this?

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:41.780
It's not daikon or wasabi.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.620
I-It's curry powder.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:49.380
There are some spices that could be 
u-used as medicine mixed into it, as well.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.650
Medicine...

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.960
There are all kinds 
of medicines in our current era,

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:58.240
but long ago they'd use this instead.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.000
That's true...

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.670
This katsu curry has a different
 meaning for me, though.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.650
What do you mean?

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.670
It can also be used to blow away hesitation

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:16.670
by saying, "With this katsu, I'll cuts 'em down!"

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.640
What, a pun?

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:26.300
When I was young, there was a restaurant

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:30.660
with real good katsu curry 
tucked away in Waseda.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:34.820
Every now and then 
I'd go there with your mother.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:36.300
Huh?

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:42.870
Ever since then, I've always gotten 
sentimental when I eat katsu curry.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:51.220
Sakuma here, at first all 
he could do was make bombs,

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:55.670
but he's learned to make 
katsu curry this delicious.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:59.890
The first katsu curry he ever 
made tasted real bad,

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:03.190
but lately the flavor's pretty guaranteed.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:07.340
Learn to make other meals, too.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:16.640
Well, we can eat our fill and regain energy, 
so I've got no complaints!

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:20.830
We're not going to lose to stupid Gibia!

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.750
Right, Doctor?

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.500
Huh? Where's the Doctor?

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:29.120
He's still conducting his research.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:33.590
I'll go take the Doctor his katsu curry.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.660
Yeah, this is good.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.000
That's great!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.300
It's Sakuma-san's best dish!

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:48.110
Apparently, the Galients have been 
eating katsu curry every day,

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:52.240
but even though they all complained, 
they ate it with joy.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.380
I see.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:57.260
Having this every day would be tough.

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:01.640
Doctor, how's the vaccine coming along?

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:04.410
Just a little more, I think.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:10.440
I thought I wouldn't be able 
to create the vaccine

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:15.930
until I went to Venice and extracted 
antibodies from patient zero,

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:19.000
but thanks to Sensui and the others

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.100
I've been able to cultivate 
a high concentration of the virus.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:25.090
So, you're using that to make the vaccine?

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:30.900
If only we'd had that, 
my mother wouldn't have had to die...

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:34.800
Doctor...

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:39.120
Please make sure to complete the vaccine!

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.500
I have faith in you!

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:44.620
We can restore the whole world!

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:53.300
<i>To restore the whole world.</i>

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.950
Oh, it's on, it's on!

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.350
Way to go!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.940
H-How's that?!

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:14.820
Th-There was a generator, 
so I-I got it back up and running!

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:20.110
With this much light the Gibia 
won't come after us, either!

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:26.580
Hmm?

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:28.700
I know!

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:34.190
Since we have the chance, 
let's do interviews!

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:40.630
I never thought I'd get to share sake 
with someone in this era.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.890
This is Aoki, a choice sake.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.490
It's really hard to get a hold of nowadays.

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:51.850
This is definitely better 
than the sake of yore.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.690
I'm excited, then.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:02.520
Honestly, I'm glad I didn't have to fight you.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:06.450
Me, too.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:07.840
Yeah.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:10.170
I wanted to try fighting him!

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:14.710
You're real good with machines, aren't you?

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:19.050
I-It's not that big a deal. 
I just like working with them.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:24.420
By the way, is that dynamite 
really so incredible?

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:25.450
Yeah!

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:29.480
O-O-Out of all the explosives, 
i-it was the invention of the century!

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:36.550
Th-The production of dynamite changed 
the history of h-human architecture.

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:38.990
Wow, really?

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:43.070
Th-Th-There were a lot 
of people who died, though.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:48.240
Man, between the bombs and the cooking,

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:50.500
you're really incredible.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:20:00.530
W-Well, the truth is, once I realized
 curry powder was similar to gunpowder,

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:03.250
I got an urge to try making it.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:07.020
Gunpowder and curry powder are similar?

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:10.310
You really are incredible!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:15.480
By the way, can you tell me 
more about bombs?

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:17.820
Sure!

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:22.480
I-I have a lot of them in our car,

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:24.360
s-so I'll show you later.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.330
Yeah!

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.990
I'm sorry.

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:34.670
I thought your mother took you 
with her and went back to China.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:39.750
She stayed in Japan, 
hoping to see you reform your life.

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:42.700
She died before she got that chance, though.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:59.030
After being in the yakuza for so long,

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:05.250
it was easier to steal 
from people than monsters.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:11.140
What you said to me 
the other day opened my eyes.

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:14.300
If you're willing to forgive me,

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:17.400
I want to spend the time 
I have left for you.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.630
I won't be able to forgive you right away.

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:28.440
Well, as long as we're together

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:30.720
I'm sure we'll come 
to understand each other.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:35.150
After all, we're a real father and daughter.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:50.490
<i>I guess this is the end of our journey.</i>

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:02.240
<i>I've gathered more than enough samples.</i>

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:47.820
Kenroku!

00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:51.730
<i>Okuni.</i>

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.810
<b>"Illusory Love"</b>
